# SIKSIK Flow Implementation Changelog

- Work period: 2026-07-16 to 2026-08-20
- Status: Unreleased local changes
- Git baseline: `ac8d1fc`
- Android agent: `0.7.0`, API `1.0`
- Primary project: `/Users/macbook/Documents/Product1/siksik`

## 2026-08-21: IG comments body text wired into analysis

- Instagram `own_comments` now merges UiDevice TextView bodies into capture
  nodes and `normalized_text` (chrome labels stripped for signature/body).
- Host social OCR cleans comment chrome before enrichment; analysis merges
  `social_snapshot_enrichments.ocr_text` into visible_ui crawl-record text and
  OCR findings so comment bodies are not skipped when a11y text is chrome-only.

## 2026-08-21: Auth-wall skip + X replies gate + FB activity hub

- Unsigned X/FB/IG sessions fail with explicit `account_not_signed_in` instead of
  a generic launch timeout. Credential Manager overlays are dismissed with Back
  (no auto-login). Host/engine map that reason to `failed`.
- X Replies require tab confirmation (`xProfileTabConfirmed` /
  `xRepliesSurfaceReady`) so Posts timeline is not stored as replies.
- Facebook comments hub accepts broader Activity Log / Your activity labels and
  verifies Comments and reactions before capture.

## 2026-08-20: Exhaust scrolls + long host timeout + TEXT_ONLY a11y preflight

- Completeness over soft budgets: IG comments, X tweets/replies, and FB
  posts/comments use exhaust scroll budgets (200) with stagnant/empty end
  detection; IG archive stays exactly 3; IG posts still page from profile
  post count with a higher grid ceiling (200).
- Host `target_timeout_s` default 1800s; navigation deadline follows that
  timeout (no 240s cap). Feed scroll/capture no longer aborts solely because
  the navigation deadline is near.
- TEXT_ONLY targets (X/FB) fail fast with `accessibility_required` when
  SIKSIK Agent accessibility is not granted before instrumentation.
- Contract/unit tests updated for exhaust constants, archive=3, and deadline
  policy. Sacred IG click ladders and scope order unchanged.

## 2026-08-20: Restore TEXT_ONLY build, all-source windows, and responsive previews

- Completed the Android TEXT_ONLY contract with shared cover/tap actions,
  Facebook/X-only cover policy, accessibility service lifecycle, bounded gesture
  dispatch, and the internal receiver. Both APK modules now compile, test, and
  assemble with the cover enabled; Instagram remains uncovered.
- Selection policy v5 now automatically includes every in-scope Android source
  kind after inventory time filtering: image, video, audio, document, SMS,
  contact, visible UI, and notification. QUICK remains a three-calendar-month
  window and FULL a six-calendar-month window. The legacy Android and active iOS
  media/document/message paths apply the same cutoff and no longer use default
  per-type count caps. QUICK video analysis no longer stops at 80 files.
- Gmail now follows every `nextPageToken` inside the mode cutoff, handles nested
  attachments, uses the bound agent runtime correctly on fallback, and defaults
  to no message-count cap. Rendered email body content is converted to escaped
  readable text; source HTML is not inserted into the preview document.
- Gallery now separates the device-facing logical path from the staging preview
  path. Nested device paths under Download resolve to the Download album and a
  `Download/<name>` display path while media still opens from its verified
  staging file. Audio, documents, text, SMS, contacts, notifications, and social
  records are included; binary canonical duplicates, screenshots, and Gmail
  metadata JSON are excluded.
- Video and audio are no longer downloaded eagerly by every Gallery/Findings
  row. A ten-minute, user/session/path-bound media ticket feeds Starlette range
  streaming only after the operator clicks the item. OCR and structured JSON
  previews extract readable text instead of rendering raw JSON. Email/PDF HTML
  previews run in a sandboxed iframe.
- Added coverage for semantic Download paths, non-image Gallery records, exact
  three/six calendar-month edges, safe email rendering, Gmail runtime fallback,
  scoped range tickets, and all eight Android selection source kinds.

## 2026-08-20: TEXT_ONLY overlay pinned + X drawer/avatar fix + FB profile proof

- Crawl evidence (session `35b2e006`): debug frames showed **no white cover** on FB/X
  and X opening a full-screen profile photo instead of the account drawer. Root cause:
  `onForegroundPackage` hid the cover on agent/automation FG switches; IG→FB handoff
  left it off. Cover is now **pinned** until an explicit hide broadcast at crawl end.
  `ensureTextOnlyCoverVisible()` re-applies show on launch, each scope, and capture.
- X: removed top-left `ImageView`/coordinate fallbacks that opened profile **media
  viewer** or other accounts. Drawer opens only via labeled
  `Tampilkan penarik navigasi` / Account menu with proof (`Profil`, `Markah`, …).
  `recoverXFromWrongSurface()` backs out of media viewer / Follow profiles.
  `xLooksLikeOtherProfile()` treats any Follow/Subscribe without Edit as foreign.
- Facebook: deferred profile verify no longer returns true without
  `hasFacebookOwnProfileProof()` (was accepting onboarding/home as profile).
- **Operator:** re-enable SIKSIK Agent accessibility after each APK install (MIUI clears it).

## 2026-08-20: Facebook profile setup wizard (Xiaomi) — skip before profile/comments

- Physical M2101K7AG: tapping `Buka profil` opens FB's new setup flow
  (`Selamat datang di profil Anda` → photo → city), not the profile wall.
  Crawler then failed comments/posts because it never reached Edit profil /
  Pengaturan profil lainnya.
- Additive universal handler: detect onboarding fragments, tap `Lewati`/`Skip`
  through multi-step setup, confirm `BERHENTI` on “Berhenti menyiapkan profil”.
  `hasFacebookOwnProfileProof()` rejects onboarding surfaces (e.g. `Edit foto profil`
  without About/Semua). Called from `navigateFacebook`, `openFacebookOwnProfile`,
  and `openFacebookMoreProfileSettings`. Infinix/Samsung profile-tab path unchanged.
- APK rebuilt and installed on `9d2bb285`. **Re-enable accessibility** for
  SIKSIK Agent in Settings → Aksesibilitas (MIUI blocks `adb settings put`).
  Overlay TEXT_ONLY putih tetap aktif sepanjang mapping FB/X.

## 2026-08-20: Facebook/X TEXT_ONLY — keep white cover, own profile, comments/likes, feed scroll

- TEXT_ONLY solid white cover stays up for the whole Facebook/X mapping,
  including the finished frame. Hide only after that snapshot, when returning
  to the agent. Instagram remains uncovered. Never `descContains("Profile")` on X.
- X own-profile proof requires Edit profile / Edit profil. Follow+Message without
  Edit is treated as someone else's profile (back out). Profil is tapped only from
  the account drawer or a bottom tab — not from home-timeline text.
- Facebook comments: Indonesian `Pengaturan profil lainnya` (and EN equivalents)
  before generic More. Activity log → Comments and reactions hub (All filter) so
  comments and likes/reactions can be captured. Generic More only if the settings
  sheet is actually visible.
- Facebook/X feed: `UiDevice.swipe` often reports success on MIUI without moving.
  If the viewport did not change, retry accessibility ACTION_SCROLL_FORWARD.
  Filter profile chrome (`Semua postingan`, Filter, Reel, composer) out of posts.
- Infinix/Samsung action-click and Instagram visual path unchanged.

## 2026-08-20: Xiaomi X/Facebook — ACTION_CLICK false-positive, a11y service-tap retry

- Physical M2101K7AG: latest crawl still `x_profile_not_verified` /
  `facebook_profile_not_verified` while Instagram scopes verified. Manual dumps
  in `temp_crawl/manual_xfb_20260820/` show the working path is
  accessibility-service tap only (`A11Y_TAP`): X `Tampilkan penarik navigasi`
  then exact `Profil` → Edit profil / Postingan / @handle; Facebook clickable
  `Buka profil` → Edit profil / Tambahkan ke cerita / Semua. Overlay TEXT_ONLY
  unchanged. Never `descContains("Profile")` on X.
- MIUI `ACTION_CLICK` and `UiObject2.click()` often return true without moving
  the UI, so the crawler skipped the real tap. Keep existing Infinix/Samsung
  action-click first. If own-profile chrome is still missing, retry the same
  labeled node with `allowActionClick=false` (service gesture only). Drawer
  `Profil` must leave the drawer; do not treat a no-op click as success.
- X Posts/Replies tab band widened from 2/3 to 4/5 of display height so tall
  Xiaomi profile chrome still counts; English/Infinix tabs stay inside the band.

## 2026-08-20: Gmail non-root acquisition via AccountManager + REST API & Gallery filter

- Added non-root Gmail acquisition to SIKSIK via Android `AccountManager` token broker and Google Gmail REST API.
- Android Agent: Added `AccountRoutes` (`/v1/accounts/google`, `/v1/accounts/google/token`) with `GET_ACCOUNTS` and `USE_CREDENTIALS` permissions to request OAuth2 Bearer token for `oauth2:https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly`.
- Backend: Implemented `GmailAcquisitionService` (`backend/app/acquisition/gmail_service.py`) to fetch message headers, plain/html body, labels, attachments, and generate rendered email HTML cards in `staging/email/`.
- Gallery & Findings: Enabled `source in {"email", "gmail"}` in `is_gallery_media` with `album="Email"`, ensuring all email messages (both flagged and non-flagged) appear in Gallery under the `Email` filter and in `Semua` (`ACCESS_ALL`).
- Added full unit and integration test suite in `backend/tests/test_gmail_acquisition.py`.

## 2026-08-19: Xiaomi trash + X/Facebook profile navigation

- Gallery Recycle on M2101K7AG keeps JPEGs in
  `/sdcard/MIUI/Gallery/cloud/.trashBin/{-trash-}*`. QUICK already finds them
  under `MIUI/`. Recover then hashed every live MediaStore path; one row is
  `/storage/emulated` (outside shared storage) and aborted the run with
  `validation_error`, so trash never landed in the report. Skip invalid live
  paths while hashing disk-cache duplicates. Infinix imgcache path unchanged.
- X Indonesian drawer is `Tampilkan penarik navigasi`, not `laci navigasi`.
  Match that exact/contains label; still never `descContains("Profile")`.
- Facebook bottom bar has no Profile tab. Use clickable `Menu` / `Buka profil`
  (a11y, then point/shell tap). Ignore the duplicate non-clickable `Buka profil`
  node. Overlay TEXT_ONLY unchanged.

## 2026-08-19: Xiaomi special access — ADB put-secure denial is not operator denial

- MIUI often returns `SecurityException` / `Permission denial` on
  `settings put secure enabled_accessibility_services`. Bootstrap treated that
  as `DENIED` and failed immediately with "Special access Android ditolak"
  without opening Accessibility settings.
- Retry once after `pm grant WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS`. If still blocked, wait on
  the Accessibility settings screen like other OEMs. Operator denial during
  that wait is still `DENIED`. Infinix/Samsung restore-success path unchanged.

## 2026-08-19: IG Xiaomi — settings deeplink, archive row, comments extra-scroll

- Archive still tries own profile first (Infinix/Samsung hamburger path). Xiaomi
  may miss the profile tab; `instagram://settings` stays last resort only.
- Physical Xiaomi M2101K7AG (`9d2bb285`): UiObject2 / UiDevice / a11y / `input tap`
  on profile `Opsi` never open Settings (INJECT_EVENTS). `instagram://settings`
  opens the same "Pengaturan dan aktivitas" sheet (Arsip / Tersimpan / Aktivitas Anda).
  Infinix/Samsung still use hamburger first; deeplink is last resort only.
- Archive: clicking `Arsip` via UiDevice returned success while still on Settings,
  then `instagramArchivePageVisible` treated the Settings "Arsip" label as the
  archive page. Require Settings to leave, click a11y first (same as comments),
  reject Settings-as-archive.
- Comments: list already opened (`Komentar` / `Terbaru ke terlama`) then
  `scope_verification_failed` because own-account was only marked after profile
  tab. Mark verified from Settings/comments chrome. Extra comment scrolls threw
  `RuntimeException` (`uiautomator dump` vs instrumentation UiAutomation) and
  marked the whole crawl `partial` after a stored capture. Keep the initial
  capture; log exception type only; screenshot-only comments/archive if a11y
  nodes are empty. Overlay unchanged.

