## 2026-08-18: iOS social apps never opened — WDA died before HTTP

- Session `ddffd953` (20:46 WIB) still had no visible_ui. Gallery/SMS/contacts
  committed; IG/X/FB never launched. `/tmp/ios-media-puller-wda.log` shows
  `ios runwda` dying at ~5s (`Failed running WDA` / DTX broken pipe to the
  go-ios tunnel). `ios forward` stayed up, so `/status` probes hit error
  code 2 (`could not connect to phone`). Apps cannot open without that HTTP
  session. This is the same stack `bee88e45` / `run_all_profiles.sh` used
  when social worked; the host was not waiting like those wrappers.
- Causes: `pkill` then `runwda` after 0.5s (XCTest session still tearing
  down); curl `/status` 2s later during IDE init; `.env`
  `IOS_WDA_HTTP_WAIT_SEC=30` overwriting the host 120s budget; Python only
  polling 20s after `run_stack.sh` exited.
- `run_stack.sh` now keeps host wait env, waits 3s after pkill, 8s for
  XCTest attach before forward/curl, retries `runwda` three times, and the
  host polls for the full boot timeout then settles 3s (same as
  `run_ig_profile.sh`). Product1 `ios-media-puller` remains reference-only.

## 2026-08-18: iOS social crawl produced no records (WDA HTTP + CLI)

- Session `af030716` (iOS QUICK) finished as `ios_afc_media+ios_backup_comms` with
  contacts/SMS only. Gallery came through; social did not. `automation.log`
  reached tunnel + developer mode + WDA bundle at 17:22 and never logged
  HTTP ready. `run_stack.sh` waited 12s boot + 30s HTTP, then exited; background
  `ios runwda` / `ios forward` were not disowned, so bash SIGHUP tore them down
  before port 8100 stayed up. Host checked HTTP once and fail-soft skipped
  social. Facebook `fb-profile` existed in the in-tree puller but was not a
  target.
- Host no longer calls `automator.py --skip-wda-install … --http … -o …`.
  Caps, WDA URL, UDID, and output dir are written to a JSON job and
  `ios_wda/invoke.py` runs the in-tree flows with the puller venv (no operator
  `--` flags). Product1 `ios-media-puller` stayed reference-only (no runtime
  path). `run_stack.sh` nohup/disowns WDA processes; host polls HTTP for the
  configured boot timeout. Facebook is included in `ios_social_targets`.
- Verification: backend unit tests for IG/X/FB record mapping and job payload.
  Physical iPhone recrawl not run in this step.

## 2026-08-18: Repair mashed Instagram Spotify profile-link OCR

- Owner-view IG profile a11y only exposes username + metrics (`profile_header_familiar_*`).
  Bio/link are not in the tree (`profile_header_link` / `bio` missing). Screenshot still
  shows `open.spotify.com/user/…`. EasyOCR emitted `open spotify comluser/31 …`; repair
  only matched `com/`, so `profile_links` stayed empty and the report showed "—".
- `repair_ocr_link_text` now restores `comluser` → `open.spotify.com/user/` and joins
  split path tokens. Reports reuse that helper, so an already-ingested session can
  show the link on refresh without recrawl.

## 2026-08-18: Social crawl failed after overlay runner swap

- Sessions `80282cd9` / `217971a5`: `accessibility_visible_ui` partial
  `ig:instrumentation_failed;x:instrumentation_failed;fb:instrumentation_failed`.
  No mapping files. Crawl row finished in ~2s. Session `1f6d7200` minutes earlier
  still had IG+FB records.
- Cause: automation APK registered only `SiksikAndroidJUnitRunner`, while a live
  backend can still invoke `androidx.test.runner.AndroidJUnitRunner`. Device then
  returns `Unable to find instrumentation` for every target, including Instagram.
- Fix: register **both** runners on the automation APK. Overlay runner stays the
  host default (`FLAG_DONT_SUPPRESS_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICES`). Stock runner remains
  so crawl still works if the backend process was not restarted.

