## 2026-07-22: Instagram Crawl Timeout Regression Fix

### Root Cause

- Diagnosed session `0542f9e7-7522-4c32-b81d-cd450815201e` from physical-device logcat.
- The Profile coordinate tap completed in 155 ms. The next `device.findObjects(By.pkg("com.instagram.android"))` call then enumerated Instagram's complete UiAutomator hierarchy and blocked until the 180-second host timeout terminated instrumentation.
- No scope had completed its initial capture before the blocked query. Therefore the agent had no social screenshot record to transfer, and the backend had nothing to mirror into `temp_crawl` or expose in the report.

### Physical Rerun Correction

- Audited the next physical dashboard run, session `d8596cd5-bf5c-4963-b54f-db49aed16bfb` / crawl `crawl_cb5abbb5-f352-4106-875f-bb582d6f6de7`.
- The complete-package hierarchy timeout was gone. The Profile coordinate tap completed in 162 ms, but the proof loop rejected the still-rendering profile after only three 350 ms probes.
- All four Instagram scopes consequently failed with `instagram_profile_not_verified`. The committed transfer correctly contained zero records and zero artifacts; this confirmed that `temp_crawl` and report persistence were downstream symptoms, not the failing component.
- Captured the physical Instagram hierarchy after render. It exposed exact own-account evidence through `Edit profile`, `Share profile`, `Your profile`, profile metrics, username resource, selected grid tab, grid items, and exact `Options`.
- Changed `Edit profile`, `Share profile`, and `Your profile` into independent strong own-account proofs. Other-account Follow-state rejection remains active.
- Replaced the three-probe 1.8-second failure window with adaptive 250 ms polling for at most six seconds. The flow exits immediately when proof appears and performs only two bounded recovery taps/Back actions.
- Added content-free proof telemetry for signal score, metric-group count, and Edit/Share visibility.
- Accepted a verified zero-post profile as a valid static Posts capture instead of reporting `instagram_own_posts_empty`.
- Increased bounded Archive/menu render polling to four seconds. The current Instagram Settings and activity page is supported in addition to the older bottom-sheet presentation; both require exact Archive plus a known companion entry.
- Verified the selection boundary: every configured own-account social scope is a required scope and is auto-selected for direct transfer even without a risk keyword. Social account data remains report data and is not converted into a finding.

### Bounded Instagram State Machine

- Removed complete-package UiAutomator enumeration from every Instagram path.
- Replaced the blocking package query with a bounded `UiAutomation.rootInActiveWindow` snapshot capped by the existing visible-node contract.
- Reduced UiAutomator idle and selector waits to bounded 250 ms and 500 ms values so animated Instagram surfaces cannot consume the default 10-second idle wait per query.
- Read the foreground package from the active accessibility root before using the bounded UiDevice fallback.
- Added content-free scope telemetry for scope start, initial capture, scroll capture, and failure reason.

### Profile and Post Grid

- Preserved the required Home-to-Profile action: tap the bottom-right Profile position first, then verify the own-account profile from bounded header, metric, username, Edit Profile, Share Profile, and grid signals.
- Removed redundant screenshot-based surface signatures from the scroll loop.
- Parsed the post count from exact post-count resources, inline count labels, or spatially adjacent count/Posts nodes.
- Kept zero additional scrolls when the post count is three or fewer.
- For larger profiles, calculated one overlapping grid scroll per additional row and captured every viewport after the initial profile/grid viewport.
- Reduced Instagram swipe animation steps from 30 to 16 and the explicit post-swipe settle to 250 ms. The backend stable interval is 300 ms.
- Added screenshot-digest duplicate detection using the screenshot already required by the flow. No additional comparison screenshot is taken.

### Story Archive

- Enforced the sequence Profile -> top-right hamburger coordinate -> verified options sheet -> exact `Archive`/`Arsip` row.
- The options sheet is accepted only when exact Archive and a known companion entry are present in the same bounded snapshot.
- Removed generic clickable/resource traversal from Archive navigation. Create, Highlight, post creation, and archive thumbnails are never candidate targets.
- Verified the archive header after entry. Posts Archive and Live Archive are switched only through the exact header and exact `Stories archive`/`Arsip cerita` dropdown option.
- Captured one initial Stories Archive viewport and at most three overlapping scroll viewports. A repeated screenshot digest stops the loop early at the bottom.

### Capture Persistence and Limits

- Kept each screenshot attached to a persisted `visible_ui` record immediately after capture. A later optional scope failure now returns a partial outcome without discarding earlier records.
- Preserved the existing direct-transfer enrichment path. Transferred Instagram screenshots are atomically mirrored to `/Users/macbook/Documents/Product1/temp_crawl/<session_id>/<crawl_id>/` before optional host OCR runs, then joined into the existing report layout.
