## 2026-07-22: Host Social OCR and Instagram Profile/Archive Correction

### Host OCR Boundary

- Moved OCR for `visible_ui` social screenshots from the Android agent to the laptop backend.
- Android still captures the scoped Instagram screenshot and runs perceptual hashing, face detection, and object detection. It emits the explicit `ocr_host_deferred` hand-off instead of running ML Kit OCR for the social screenshot.
- Added one reusable host OCR backend per direct-transfer operation. EasyOCR receives bounded 1280-pixel input, a 1.25 magnification ratio, no forced upscaling, and no sharpening.
- Added OCR bounding boxes to the backend OCR result contract. Instagram counts are paired with `posts`, `followers`, and `following` labels by bounded horizontal and vertical distance instead of OCR line order.
- Reused the host OCR result during image analysis. Social screenshots are not OCR-processed twice.
- Kept X/Twitter text-only. X does not create screenshots and does not enter the host screenshot OCR path.

### Debug Snapshot Mirror

- Added an atomic, best-effort debug mirror for transferred Instagram screenshots under `/Users/macbook/Documents/Product1/temp_crawl/<session_id>/<crawl_id>/`.
- Debug filenames include platform, social scope, capture index, record ID, and artifact ID.
- The debug mirror is outside canonical forensic staging. It does not change record hashes, manifests, transfer receipts, selection decisions, or evidence paths.
- Added `SADT_ANDROID_SOCIAL_DEBUG_SNAPSHOTS` and `SADT_ANDROID_SOCIAL_DEBUG_DIR` configuration. Debug mirroring is enabled by default for the current local build.

### Profile Metadata

- Added exact Instagram profile evidence queries for `action_bar_title`, post count, follower count, following count, bio, and profile-link resources when the accessibility root contains only a window placeholder.
- Prioritized resource-backed metadata before host OCR fallback. The report stores the canonical username without `@`; the existing frontend renders it as `@<username>`.
- Added spatial host OCR fallback for profile username and metrics. Header-position selection prevents Instagram Notes text from replacing the account username.
- Added `.blog` to bio-link recognition. Values such as `ltfzp.blog` are retained as profile links and rejected as username candidates.
- Added report enrichment overlay for historical/canonical records without mutating their JSON files.

### Story Archive Navigation

- Removed the remaining unbounded `By.clickable(true)` fallback from the Instagram profile-menu selector.
- The hamburger path now accepts only verified Options labels/resources, followed by the bounded top-right coordinate fallback.
- Kept Create, Highlight, Threads, Settings, and professional controls on the exclusion list.
- Archive entry requires a verified options sheet containing exact Archive/Arsip plus a known companion entry.
- Generic Archive is accepted only as the archive page entry header. Capture starts only after the mode is verified as exact Stories Archive/Arsip Cerita or switched through the archive dropdown.
- Archive thumbnails remain unopened. The capture boundary remains one initial screenshot plus at most three overlapping scroll screenshots.

### Runtime Stability

- Stopped force-stopping the automation package after a successful, already-completed instrumentation run. Timeout, cancellation, and failed instrumentation still use forced cleanup.
- Restored the main agent and previously granted Accessibility state after instrumentation without repeatedly opening Android Settings.
- Added a silent Accessibility restore attempt before presenting Settings when the backend observes a transient not-granted state.
- Reduced redundant Instagram profile waits and retries while keeping bounded navigation and verification.
- Diagnosed session `be6ff5a0-8afd-464d-872c-81acde40df86`: Instagram launched successfully, instrumentation stayed alive, no profile tap was injected, and the target ended with `automation_timeout` and zero social records.
- Reordered Home navigation so the bounded bottom-right Profile coordinate tap occurs before any Instagram hierarchy proof or dialog scan.
- Replaced package hierarchy checks in launch/foreground stabilization with deterministic current-package polling and fixed bounded settle intervals.
- Replaced dozens of sequential Home selectors with one bounded package-hierarchy pass per proof attempt.
- Limited initial Instagram profile navigation to an internal 8-second budget instead of allowing it to consume the 180-second outer ADB timeout.
- Deferred dialog dismissal until a failed profile tap produces an exact known dismiss target in the same hierarchy pass.
- Avoided the redundant shared scope-ledger clear between successful target launch and first scope navigation.
