## Scope and Architecture

- SIKSIK remains the primary application and runtime authority.
- `Flow.md` defines the required Android acquisition pipeline.
- LPDP was used only as a code and design donor. SIKSIK has no LPDP runtime dependency.
- `forensics-refrences` was reviewed only. No root, exploit, decryption, or private-app database code was imported.
- Existing SIKSIK backend, analysis, findings, review, recommendation, RBAC, report, and UI flows remain authoritative.
- Android hand-off uses canonical JSON records, a manifest, and individually verified files.
- The Android agent does not create ZIP archives.
- The existing SIKSIK ZIP upload provider remains available and unchanged.
- Existing frontend routes, layout, stylesheet, and visual conventions were preserved.

