## Phase 02: Android Agent

### Main APK

- Package: `com.siksik.agent`.
- Version: `0.7.0`, version code 7.
- minSdk 26, compileSdk 35, targetSdk 35.
- Java and Kotlin target 17.
- Runs a foreground service with a loopback-only HTTP server on `127.0.0.1:38471`.
- Validates session ID, token, and expiration before starting the service.
- Uses session-bound bearer authentication and request IDs.
- Uses bounded request bodies, responses, workers, and timeouts.
- Reports capabilities only after real initialization and health checks succeed.
- Cleans session secrets and private runtime state on stop or expiration.
- Uses a minimal white Android activity.

### Automation APK

- Package: `com.siksik.agent.automation`.
- Runs UiAutomator as a separate instrumentation APK.
- Main and automation APKs use the same shared UID for the protected communication capture store.
- Refactored the automation source set to compile only automation code and shared communication contracts.
- Fixed the build failure caused by compiling the full main-agent source tree without its dependencies.

### Agent APIs

Added authenticated routes for:

- session bootstrap, capabilities, health, and stop;
- permissions and grants;
- media catalog and thumbnails;
- inventory start, status, paging, cancel, and resume;
- social automation results;
- preprocessing start, status, paging, and cancel;
- selection, candidates, live-selected records, mutation, confirmation, and cancel;
- direct transfer, manifest, status, cleanup, and receipts.

## Phase 03: Automatic ADB Bootstrap

Implemented this state machine:

`detect → validate → build/reuse APK → inspect package → install/update → grant runtime permissions → verify special access → start agent → create forward → authenticated handshake → ready`

Changes:

- Backend builds or reuses both APKs automatically.
- Main APK installation uses `adb install -r -g`.
- Automation APK installation uses `adb install -r -t`.
- Installed package version, signer, and identity are verified.
- Matching agent installations are reused without reinstalling.
- ADB forwarding uses a dynamic host port mapped to device port 38471.
- Handshake validates session, package, API, agent version, Android API, and build identity.
- Forwarding and runtime processes are cleaned on failure, cancellation, teardown, and backend shutdown.

### Installation Migration

Handled:

- `INSTALL_FAILED_UID_CHANGED`;
- `INSTALL_FAILED_SHARED_USER_INCOMPATIBLE`;
- `INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE`.

For UID/shared-user migration, the installer removes only the configured old agent package and retries once. A one-time uninstall clears Android grants, so Accessibility must be approved again after this migration.

### Permission Flow

- Runtime media, audio, SMS, contact, notification, and media-location permissions are applied through `-g` and `pm grant` where supported.
- Accessibility requires user approval in Android Settings.
- Storage/All files is requested only when full shared-storage scanning requires it.
- Notification Listener is granted through `cmd notification allow_listener` when supported.
- Notification state is probed up to three times for OEM propagation delays.
- Normal phone interaction is limited to Accessibility and optional full-scan Storage approval.
- Previously granted Accessibility state is captured before instrumentation and restored for the active Android user afterward.

### OEM and Connection Recovery

- Fixed Infinix Settings false failures from `am start -W` output containing `Activity not started` for an already-running Settings activity.
- Exit code, `Status: ok`, delivered-intent output, and explicit failure markers are now evaluated separately.
- Missing activities, unresolved intents, security exceptions, permission denials, and non-zero exits still fail.
- Restarts the main agent after each social instrumentation target.
- Added coordinated loopback recovery for temporary agent or ADB-forward loss.
- Recovery uses a lock and generation counter to prevent concurrent duplicate repairs.

## Phase 04: Media and Document Inventory

Added these inventory adapters:

| Adapter | Scope |
| --- | --- |
| `media_store_image` | Images and image metadata |
| `media_store_video` | Videos, dimensions, duration, timestamps |
| `media_store_audio` | Audio and duration |
| `shared_storage_document` | PDF, DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX, CSV, TXT, RTF |
| `document_tree` | Recursive user-granted document tree |
| `public_whatsapp` | Public WhatsApp media directories |
| `public_telegram` | Public Telegram media directories |

Inventory behavior:

- Uses MediaStore and DocumentsContract only.
- Does not read private application sandboxes.
- Captures normalized timestamps, dimensions, duration, directory hints, EXIF, camera fields, and GPS where available.
- Preserves public-app provenance before generic MediaStore deduplication.
- Stores cursors and checkpoints in the private agent database.
- Exposes opaque cursor tokens only.
- Quick mode performs bounded sampling and reports `sampled`.
- Full mode consumes all accessible source cursors to terminal state.
- Reports denied, restricted, unsupported, partial, cancelled, and failed sources explicitly.
- Current page limits:
  - media/public/document: 100;
  - SMS: 64;
  - contacts: 100;
  - visible UI: 1;
  - notifications: 50.

## Phase 05: Communication and Social Crawling

### Communication Sources

- Added SMS ContentProvider inventory with bounded text and stable checkpoints.
- Added batched contact inventory without N+1 detail queries.
- Added session-bound Accessibility visible-UI capture.
- Added session-bound Notification Listener capture with stable update/removal identities.
- Limited visible trees to depth 16, 256 nodes, and 512 characters per node field.
- Limited SMS text to 32,768 characters and contact normalized text to 8,192 characters.
- Limited capture records to 5,000 per type/session.
- Blocked Instagram, X, and Facebook notifications to prevent DM, recommendation, like, and follow data from bypassing social scope controls.

### Active Social Targets

Default targets:

- `com.instagram.android`;
- `com.twitter.android`.

Facebook remains in the compatibility registry but is not enabled by default.

Allowed scopes:

- `own_profile`;
- `own_posts`;
- `own_tweets`;
- `own_story_archive`;
- `own_comments`;
- `own_replies`.

Home feeds, recommendations, other profiles, DMs, likes, follows, posting, deletion, purchases, credential input, and private target-app databases are excluded.

### Instagram

- Verifies the logged-in profile through the profile tab and Edit Profile marker.
- Captures visible username, bio, and profile links.
- Opens grid posts individually.
- Verifies post ownership against the profile account marker when available.
- Uses visited signatures to prevent duplicate post capture.
- Opens Archive, selects Story Archive, and opens an archive item before capture.
- Advances archive stories with a right-side tap and requires a changed, unvisited signature.
- Opens account comments through Your Activity → Interactions → Comments.
- Crops profile and post screenshots to the verified scope.

### X / Twitter

- Opens the account drawer and Profile.
- Verifies Edit Profile and the current account handle.
- Captures visible handle, bio, and profile links.
- Selects Posts and Replies explicitly.
- Opens only items containing the verified account marker.
- Opens items individually.
- Processes all unvisited items on the current screen before scrolling.
- Uses signatures to prevent duplicate tweet/reply capture.
- Rejects generic thread content when account ownership cannot be proven.
- Crops screenshots to verified own-account content.

### White Screen Behavior

- Local inventory, preprocessing, selection, and transfer preparation can run behind the white SIKSIK activity.
- Instagram/X must be foreground during UiAutomator and Accessibility inspection.
- The target application is therefore visible during bounded social crawling.
- Automation always returns to the white SIKSIK activity after success, timeout, cancellation, missing target, or failure.
- API 34 privacy curtain and API 33 text-only white mode are not implemented.

## Phase 06: Local Android Preprocessing

| Capability | Engine |
| --- | --- |
| OCR | ML Kit Latin bundled 16.0.1 |
| Document extraction | SIKSIK bounded parser + Apache POI 5.5.1 |
| Exact hash | Streaming SHA-256 |
| Perceptual hash | 64-bit dHash |
| Face detection | BlazeFace short-range float16 |
| Face embedding | MobileNet V3 Small float32, 1,024 dimensions |
| Object detection | EfficientDet-Lite0 int8 |
| Vision runtime | MediaPipe Tasks Vision 0.10.35 |

Processing map:

- images: SHA-256, dHash, OCR, face, object;
- videos: SHA-256 plus bounded representative-frame visual processing;
- audio: SHA-256 and source metadata;
- documents: SHA-256 and text extraction;
- PDF: page render followed by OCR;
- SMS, contacts, notifications: normalized typed source text;
- visible UI: node text plus record-bound screenshot OCR/face/object/dHash.

Supported documents:

- PDF;
- DOC/DOCX;
- XLS/XLSX;
- CSV;
- TXT;
- RTF.

Current limits:

- 3 preprocessing workers;
- 20-second standard item timeout;
- 120-second full-mode document timeout;
- 10-minute quick deadline;
- 6-hour full deadline;
- 4 million shared visual pixels;
- 4 GiB exact-hash/stage file limit;
- 32 MiB document input;
- 24 PDF pages;
- 32,768 OCR characters and 128 OCR regions;
- 65,536 document text characters;
- 8 face signals and 12 object labels per record.

Optimizations:

- Decodes a bounded visual base once for dHash, OCR, face, and object processing.
- Added exact-content caches keyed by source kind, MIME, and SHA-256.
- Cache limits: 64 visual results and 32 document results.
- Failed or cancelled results are not cached.
- Cache hits are marked with `content_hash_cache_hit`.
- Added deterministic exact/perceptual duplicate clustering.
- Added bounded BK-tree perceptual grouping with Hamming distance 8.
- Added anonymous face clustering with cosine similarity 0.92.
- Raw face vectors remain private and are deleted after cluster membership is applied.

## Phase 07: Selection and Review

- Added backend-owned `siksik-selection-v3` policy generation.
- The APK does not contain a second production risk dictionary.
- Policy fingerprint is validated before use.
- Threshold: 5,500 basis points, inclusive.
- Quick budget: 2,500 candidates, 1 GiB.
- Full budget: 10,000 candidates, 8 GiB.
- Added normalized phrase/token keyword matching with alphanumeric boundaries.
- Added source, text, keyword, face, and object scoring.
- Added deterministic duplicate representative handling.
- All verified own-account social scopes are selected for reporting even without a keyword match.
- Added private candidate ledger, revision control, expected-revision conflicts, idempotent confirmation, and immutable confirmed revisions.
- `review_candidates=false` auto-confirms.
- `review_candidates=true` waits for operator/admin review.
- Agent selection does not create findings or recommendations.

### Incremental Selection

- Preprocessing and selection run concurrently after inventory reaches terminal state.
- SMS, contacts, notifications, visible UI, and documents become selection inputs as each record finishes.
- Images and videos wait for final duplicate/face clustering to prevent unstable representatives.
- Added cursor-based `live-selected-records` endpoint.
- Backend reads pages of 16 and analyzes batches up to 64 records.
- Live ingestion is disabled during manual candidate review.

Current limitation: incremental analysis begins after inventory completes, not while inventory enumeration is still running.

## Phase 08: Direct Transfer Without ZIP

Implemented:

`confirmed selection → private stage → manifest → canonical record and selected attachments → one recursive ADB pull → size/hash validation → database commit → cleanup receipt`

- Only confirmed selection revisions can be staged.
- Canonical records use `application/vnd.siksik.crawl-record+json`.
- Original binary files are included only for selected media/documents.
- Screenshots are included only for selected visible-UI records.
- Manifest binds session, crawl, policy, revision, selection fingerprint, record, role, MIME, path, size, and SHA-256.
- Rejects absolute paths, traversal, symlinks, ZIP paths, duplicate IDs, relation mismatches, count mismatches, size mismatches, and hash mismatches.
- Commits records, artifacts, and transfer receipt transactionally.
- Requests agent cleanup only after the server receipt is committed.
- Reuses verified hashes and canonical timestamps during indexing.

### Server Storage Behavior

For Android-agent sessions:

- Full inventory and preprocessing intermediate data remain on Android.
- Unselected source binaries are not copied to server staging.
- Server stores bounded runtime/event metadata, candidate ledger metadata, selected canonical records, selected binaries/screenshots, findings, and reports.
- Live ingestion writes only auto-selected canonical records.
- Final transfer writes only selected artifacts.

The legacy ZIP provider keeps its original storage behavior.

## Phase 09: SIKSIK Analysis Integration

- Parses canonical records through strict `InventoryRecordV1` validation.
- Analyzes only canonical `normalized_text`; JSON keys and raw metadata are not keyword-scanned.
- Sends image/video/screenshot artifacts through the existing SIKSIK visual analyzer.
- Preserves existing findings, review, and recommendation authority.
- Adds source app, social scope, record ID, timestamps, artifact role, and acquisition method to file metadata.
- Runs live-selected analysis under session status `ACQUIRING`.
- Publishes findings before the full session is terminal.
- Processes only `files.analyzed = 0`, allowing safe incremental calls.
- Commits analyzed state and findings in batches before publishing progress.
- Accumulates live-analysis time into final analysis timing.
- OCR, keyword analysis, crawling, selection, and L1/L2 findings do not require an LLM.

### SQLite Concurrency Fix

Fixed `cannot start a transaction within a transaction` by:

- serializing all connection operations with one `asyncio.Lock`;
- using the same lock for execute, executemany, fetch, and transaction operations;
- closing cursors explicitly;
- rolling back on `BaseException`, including cancellation;
- committing only after a successful transaction block.

## Phase 10: Frontend and Report Integration

No frontend stylesheet or route was replaced.

### Live Telemetry

- Added `preparing_agent`, `awaiting_access`, `selecting`, and `awaiting_review` session states.
- Mapped the new states into the existing Acquisition pipeline step.
- Polls active sessions every 500 ms.
- Updates the local total/phase clock every 500 ms.
- Displays committed transfer/live-file counts under `MASUK`.
- Displays processed OCR count and OCR hit count separately.
- Publishes live file counts before analysis starts.
- Publishes analyzed/finding counts only after database commit.
- Refreshes the open Findings or Report page when live counts increase.
- Uses a polling epoch to prevent stale session responses from overwriting the current session.

### Finding Preview

- Added optional `preview_path` and `preview_text` fields.
- Resolves a verified image/video artifact from the same crawl record.
- Uses normalized text or bounded evidence when no media preview exists.
- Limits text preview to 320 characters.
- Does not display raw `.siksik-record.json` content.
- Falls back to text when image/video loading fails.

### Social Report

- Added `social_accounts` and `social_data` to JSON/HTML reports.
- Groups data by Instagram and X.
- Includes username/handle, visible bio, and up to 16 profile links.
- Includes scope, observation time, and normalized preview for social items.
- Separates social account data from findings.
- Limits rendered social items to 500 and exposes truncation metadata.
- Reuses existing SIKSIK frontend classes for desktop and mobile layouts.

## Phase 11–12: Hardening and Performance

- Increased inventory page sizes to reduce loopback round trips.
- Added 4 MiB default response ceiling to fix `records=too_long`.
- Reused one visual decode across four preprocessors.
- Added exact-content inference caches.
- Batched direct-transfer and analysis database writes.
- Performs one recursive ADB pull followed by per-file verification.
- Increased full social navigation budget to 24 operations per target.
- Quick social navigation remains 3 operations per target.
- Screenshot budgets: quick 6, full 16 per target.
- Preprocessing and selection polling interval: 250 ms.
- Added a read-only full-scan benchmark requiring the same device, dataset, scope, and timing boundaries.
- No faster-than-Cellebrite claim has been made.

## Defects Fixed

| Defect | Fix |
| --- | --- |
| Infinix `special_access_settings_open` false failure | Parse exit code, status, delivered intent, and hard-failure markers separately |
| `InventoryPageV1 ... records=too_long` | 4 MiB response ceiling and source-specific pagination |
| Automation build compiled the full app source tree | Restricted automation source set to shared contracts/store only |
| `INSTALL_FAILED_UID_CHANGED` | One-time configured-package uninstall and retry |
| Agent unreachable after social instrumentation | Agent restart and coordinated ADB-forward recovery |
| Repeated Accessibility prompt | Active-user exact-component probe and previous-state restoration |
| Nested SQLite transaction error | Global operation lock and cancellation-safe rollback |
| Live `MASUK/DIANALISIS` remained zero | Publish committed live-ingestion and analysis counters incrementally |
| Canonical JSON finding had no preview | Resolve related verified media or bounded normalized text |
| Instagram stopped at profile/archive page | Open individual grid posts and Story Archive items |
| Instagram repeated the same story | Before/after signature and visited-story set |
| X skipped visible account items | Process unvisited on-screen items before scrolling |
| Social notifications expanded collection scope | Reject social packages at notification listener and storage boundaries |
| Identical media repeated expensive inference | Exact SHA-256 bounded result cache |

