## Dynamic Android APK Installation Compatibility

- Replaced the single-path APK install behavior with an output-driven install policy shared by the main agent and automation APK.
- Preserved `adb install -r -g` as the preferred main-agent path and `adb install -r -t` as the preferred automation path.
- Added automatic retry without `-g` when an OEM removes the shell `INSTALL_GRANT_RUNTIME_PERMISSIONS` capability. Runtime permissions are still applied and verified individually after installation.
- Added automatic `--no-streaming` retry for bounded ADB streaming transport failures such as broken pipes, connection resets, protocol faults, and unexpected EOF.
- Preserved `-t` when the automation APK changes from streamed install to no-streaming install.
- Kept UID/shared-user and signature migration package-scoped. Only the configured incompatible SIKSIK package is uninstalled before one verified retry.
- Added typed classification for update incompatibility, UID incompatibility, insufficient storage, version downgrade, API/ABI incompatibility, user-restricted installation, device policy, invalid APK, streaming transport failure, and unknown failure.
- OEM installation approval remains an explicit Android prerequisite. The backend reports it as actionable and retryable instead of returning the generic agent-install failure.
- Applied one total installation deadline across all fallback attempts and migration work. Retry combinations cannot multiply the configured timeout.
- Persisted manufacturer, model, Android API, successful install strategy, attempt count, and install-time grant mode in redacted runtime metadata.
- Added structured `agent_install_fallback` logging with reason, selected fallback, and retry count. Raw serials, package-manager output, and device content are not logged.
- Added deterministic contract coverage for runtime-grant fallback, streamed-to-push fallback, automation `-t` preservation, OEM restriction classification, and existing UID migration behavior.
- Physical diagnostic on a Xiaomi M2101K7AG running Android 11/MIUI 12.5 confirmed two distinct OEM behaviors: `-g` was rejected by shell policy, then the no-`-g` install reached Package Installer and was blocked by the device's Install via USB policy. No successful installation or crawl was claimed from that diagnostic.
- Confirmed that the same MIUI build can report `GRANT_RUNTIME_PERMISSIONS` as granted in `dumpsys` while still rejecting both install-time grants and `pm grant` at execution time. Static shell capability output is therefore not trusted as install/grant readiness.
- Added an in-memory, per-device runtime-grant capability cache. After one verified shell-policy rejection, remaining permission checks do not repeat slow failing `pm grant` commands.
- Added an app-owned runtime-permission probe receiver. The backend now reads the agent's own effective permission state through one serial-pinned explicit broadcast instead of relying on slow and OEM-dependent `dumpsys package` output.
- Kept the permission probe payload fixed and content-free. It reports only `granted`, `denied`, or `unsupported` for the declared SIKSIK permission allowlist and never returns device content or identifiers.
- Kept legacy compatibility: if an older installed APK does not provide the probe receiver or returns an incomplete contract, the backend falls back to the bounded package-dump parser.
- Added a 500 ms in-memory permission snapshot cache to avoid repeating the same device query while bootstrap evaluates multiple permission requirements. The cache is invalidated after install and after a successful shell grant.
- Added `awaiting_runtime_permission` between runtime permission setup and special-access verification.
- When required media/storage permission cannot be granted through ADB, the backend opens the standard package-scoped Android App info screen, publishes awaiting access, and polls the exact required permissions for the active Android user.
- Bootstrap continues only after Android reports every required storage/media permission as granted. Unsupported permission contracts fail immediately; unresolved user confirmation times out with a retryable storage-access error.
- Optional SMS, contact, media-location, and notification permission failures do not create extra phone-side screens.
- Added contract coverage for capability-cache behavior, permission-probe parsing, explicit serial-pinned probe execution without `dumpsys`, and the complete denied-to-interactive-to-granted storage flow.

## Public API Changes

Added:

- `POST /api/v1/agent/bootstrap`
- `GET /api/v1/agent/status`
- `GET /api/v1/sessions/{session_id}/crawl`
- `GET /api/v1/sessions/{session_id}/candidates`
- `PATCH /api/v1/sessions/{session_id}/candidates/{record_id}`
- `POST /api/v1/sessions/{session_id}/candidates/confirm`

Additive model fields include:

- agent/bootstrap state;
- inventory/preprocessing/selection/transfer progress;
- `review_candidates`;
- finding preview fields;
- social report data.

Existing endpoints, including `/sessions/from-zip`, remain available.

